  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Potential for frost tonight across the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n1036mb sfc high continues to sit acrs the north and west tonight\nwith clear skies and light winds, leading to frost and river\nvalley fog. Given a modifying airmass temps are not expected to\nbe as low as this morning but northern areas could definitely\ndrop to the freezing mark.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A coastal low could impact at least Downeast\nMaine late this week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA coastal low is expected to develop across the Mid-Atlantic\nregion later this week while high pressure remains centered over\nQuebec. The track of the ocean low is still uncertain with \nblocking high pressure to the northwest of our forecast area and\nridging across the Great Lakes. Uncertainty remains in how \nclose the low will pass to the coast which will determine how \nfar north the precipitation will reach. Northerly to \nnortheasterly winds could become gusty over the weekend, \nespecially along the coast, as a tight pressure gradient forms. \nGeneral trend currently is that the low pressure system will \ncontinue to move southwards due to the high pressure, with \nmajority of the rain staying over the waters and the Downeast \nregion.",
